1
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:11,967
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:35,167
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:41,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,267
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:47,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,233
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:53,667
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,733
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,533 --> 00:01:00,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:02,133
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:06,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:09,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,633
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:13,367
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,367 --> 00:01:14,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:21,867
<i> We've got a search warrant</i>

21
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:24,400
<i>for the Zafras'
jewelry workshop.</i>

22
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:25,700
<i>Bring all of these
to the station.</i>

23
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,033
<i> You have to steal the gold</i>

24
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:28,700
<i>before it gets to
the safe house.</i>

25
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,733
<i>Give us 200,000
for the down payment</i>

26
00:01:30,733 --> 00:01:32,667
<i>and I will deliver you
the gold myself.</i>

27
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:34,667
<i>Domingo, transfer the gold
from your precinct</i>

28
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:36,133
<i> to the NLEA safe house.</i>

29
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:39,033
<i>Make sure the gold gets
to the safe house.</i>

30
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:40,733
<i>Sir, permission to join
the convoy.</i>

31
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:41,933
<i> Bring your team.</i>

32
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:43,567
<i>What are you doing here
in Paradise?</i>

33
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:46,533
<i>We have a big transaction.
We're talking about gold.</i>

34
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:48,067
<i>I don't think
I can accept your offer.</i>

35
00:01:48,067 --> 00:01:49,233
<i> I'm a changed man now.</i>

36
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:51,833
<i>You also know
what turning him down means.</i>

37
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:53,433
<i>The way he was looking
at Gloria...</i>

38
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:55,567
<i>I won't let him get
anywhere near Gloria.</i>

39
00:01:55,567 --> 00:01:57,933
<i> They beat up Papa!</i>

40
00:01:57,933 --> 00:01:59,200
<i> Gabo, we need your help.</i>

41
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,700
<i>Save the kids.
I'll save Mister Babot!</i>

42
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:06,833
Ahh!

43
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:08,067
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GABO GRUNTING]

44
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:10,067
[BLOWS LAND]

45
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:12,733
[BLOWS LANDING]

46
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:14,533
- Enough!
- Please!

47
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:15,600
[GABO GRUNTING]

48
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:17,700
- [YELLS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

49
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,033
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [GABO GRUNTING]

50
00:02:22,033 --> 00:02:24,267
- [MAN] Bring him here!
- [BABOT] Help!

51
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:26,600
- Enough!
- [YELLS]

52
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,867
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GABO GRUNTING]

53
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:31,767
- Enough!
- Gabo!

54
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:33,833
[WOMAN] Please, have mercy!

55
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:37,167
[GABO GRUNTING]

56
00:02:41,767 --> 00:02:48,667
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

57
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:55,033
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GABO GRUNTING]

58
00:02:57,133 --> 00:02:58,533
[BLOW LANDS]

59
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:05,000
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

60
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,067
[MAN] Go ahead!

61
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,900
Take him out!

62
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:10,967
[WOMAN CRYING]

63
00:03:10,967 --> 00:03:12,067
Gabo!

64
00:03:12,067 --> 00:03:15,267
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

65
00:03:15,267 --> 00:03:17,300
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

66
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,033
Where's Gabo?!

67
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:25,633
- Gabo!
- [GUNSHOTS]

68
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:30,667
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

69
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:34,033
[GUNSHOTS]

70
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:38,667
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

71
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:40,100
Let's go all out!

72
00:03:40,933 --> 00:03:42,300
Even if we die!

73
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,333
[GUNSHOTS]

74
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:50,233
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

75
00:03:58,133 --> 00:03:59,633
[GUNSHOTS]

76
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:00,833
Boss, we're screwed!

77
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:02,000
Let's get out of here!

78
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,333
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

79
00:04:08,333 --> 00:04:09,633
[CRYING]

80
00:04:09,633 --> 00:04:11,667
[GUNSHOTS]

81
00:04:11,667 --> 00:04:12,733
- Gabo!
- Hurry!

82
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:14,167
- Gabo!
- [GUNSHOTS]

83
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:16,200
- Hurry!
- Let's go!

84
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,833
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

85
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:20,933
Hurry up!

86
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:23,867
- Let's go!
- Hang on!

87
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:28,167
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

88
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,167
- Gabo, you can do this!
- Help!

89
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:36,233
- Somebody help us!
- Hang on, Gabo!

90
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:37,567
[MUSIC FADES]

91
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:41,400
[SIREN WAILING]

92
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:48,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:04:49,667 --> 00:04:52,200
[SIREN WAILING]

94
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,333
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [THUDS]

95
00:04:58,233 --> 00:05:00,367
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- What happened?

96
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,767
Someone got run over.

97
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,767
Hey, watch the gold.

98
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:06,100
Call for backup!

99
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:11,767
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:05:12,367 --> 00:05:13,833
[GUNSHOTS]

101
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:18,633
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

102
00:05:18,633 --> 00:05:19,733
Let's go!

103
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:23,100
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

104
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,900
[GUNSHOTS]

105
00:05:26,033 --> 00:05:27,100
[GUNSHOTS]

106
00:05:27,767 --> 00:05:28,867
Hurry!

107
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:33,267
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

108
00:05:33,267 --> 00:05:34,367
Move!

109
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:42,767
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

110
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:46,767
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

111
00:05:46,767 --> 00:05:48,167
[SIRENS WAILING]

112
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:50,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [MAX] Nobody move!

113
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:59,267
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

114
00:06:01,833 --> 00:06:02,933
Estrella!

115
00:06:02,933 --> 00:06:09,133
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

116
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:12,300
- [MAX GRUNTS]
- Go ahead!

117
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,800
I'll kill you!

118
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,267
- Jacinto!
- Don't fire!

119
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:16,433
I'll finish this!

120
00:06:17,833 --> 00:06:19,000
- What?
- Max!

121
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:25,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

122
00:06:26,333 --> 00:06:27,833
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [DJANGO GRUNTS]

123
00:06:30,467 --> 00:06:32,133
[UMALI] Open fire! Open fire!

124
00:06:32,133 --> 00:06:37,100
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

125
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:42,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:06:43,833 --> 00:06:44,933
[DJANGO] Hurry!

127
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:49,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

128
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,200
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

129
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:55,333
Enough, Max! Enough!
They didn't get the gold.

130
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,867
Did you recognize the person
who grabbed you?

131
00:06:58,867 --> 00:07:00,833
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

132
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,000
Come on!

133
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,800
Let's get back to
transferring the gold!

134
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:13,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:16,300
- [TEKLA] Uncle Rudy!
- [IPE] Uncle Rudy!

136
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:19,233
- Help! Help!
- Hurry!

137
00:07:19,233 --> 00:07:20,567
[IPE] Hurry!

138
00:07:20,567 --> 00:07:22,833
- [TEKLA] Uncle Rudy!
- What's that?

139
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,067
Maybe it's Gabo.

140
00:07:24,067 --> 00:07:25,233
Come on! Let's check on them!

141
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,200
- What happened?
- [BINOY] Uncle Rudy, help!

142
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:31,133
- [TEKLA] Uncle Rudy!
- Gabo's hurt!

143
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:38,067
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:07:51,767 --> 00:07:52,767
What happened?!

145
00:07:52,767 --> 00:07:54,700
- Help! Help!
- Gabo!

146
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,033
What happened to my son?!

147
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:57,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:59,433
- Gabo!
- I'll go first!

149
00:07:59,433 --> 00:08:00,600
Oh my god!

150
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,700
- Get inside!
- [BONG] To his room!

151
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:04,700
He was involved
in a fight again, for sure.

152
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,800
- He got hurt badly.
- [MAMENG] Who did this to him?

153
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,967
- [BINOY] To his room!
- [MAMENG] Gabo!

154
00:08:08,967 --> 00:08:10,367
[BINOY] Hang on, Gabo!

155
00:08:11,633 --> 00:08:13,067
- [RUDY] Careful.
- [BONG] Gabo, hang in there.

156
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:14,900
- Put him on the bed.
- Slowly.

157
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:16,467
- Lay him on the bed.
- God, what happened?

158
00:08:16,467 --> 00:08:17,500
Man, let's turn him.

159
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:25,167
[BINOY] We'll leave him to you.

160
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:27,067
- Gabo.
- Dan... Dante.

161
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:29,667
Please get the med kit.

162
00:08:29,667 --> 00:08:32,600
We need to clean his wounds.
Go! Hurry!

163
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,733
Yes, I'll be quick.

164
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:39,867
I knew it.

165
00:08:40,633 --> 00:08:42,433
We shouldn't have told Gabo.

166
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:43,767
We can fight
those guys ourselves!

167
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:45,567
Tekla,

168
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:47,667
we couldn't beat
those guys without Gabo.

169
00:08:47,667 --> 00:08:49,600
Look what just happened!

170
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,000
You left him alone!

171
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Tekla, we didn't
leave him alone.

172
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,900
There were so many of them.

173
00:08:55,933 --> 00:08:57,767
Good thing we saw Gabo.

174
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:59,833
Or else
they would've killed him.

175
00:08:59,833 --> 00:09:01,600
Don't say that.

176
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,267
Gabo will be fine.

177
00:09:03,267 --> 00:09:04,600
He's not going to die!

178
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,167
He really won't!

179
00:09:06,167 --> 00:09:08,100
Because if something bad
happens to Gabo,

180
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,767
I'll hunt and kill them myself!

181
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:17,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:21,600
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

183
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:25,567
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

184
00:09:30,867 --> 00:09:32,167
[BETCHAY SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

185
00:09:38,167 --> 00:09:39,833
Oh, Betchay.

186
00:09:40,733 --> 00:09:42,033
Seems like
you're going home early.

187
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,800
The people at home
pisses me off.

188
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,533
Even the ones inside BeerGin.

189
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:51,867
Am I the problem, or is it just
the people around me?

190
00:09:51,867 --> 00:09:55,200
Betchay, you're not the problem.

191
00:09:56,733 --> 00:09:57,833
If I were you,

192
00:09:59,533 --> 00:10:00,900
I'd take a day off.

193
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:02,267
Don't come in to work.

194
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:07,567
Sure, thanks. I'll get going.

195
00:10:07,567 --> 00:10:08,867
Hold on.

196
00:10:09,667 --> 00:10:13,100
I'll let you take a day off
but not alone.

197
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,833
I'll come with you.

198
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:18,567
We'll get rid of everything
that's stressing you out.

199
00:10:20,933 --> 00:10:22,233
Romy,

200
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:24,833
cover Betchay's shift
at the bar.

201
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:26,033
Okay.

202
00:10:26,033 --> 00:10:28,967
Enjoy your alone time
with Betchay.

203
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,200
[DOOR OPENS]

204
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,367
- Sir.
- Oh.

205
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:39,633
Sir.

206
00:10:39,633 --> 00:10:41,800
You successfully
turned over the evidence.

207
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,300
- Good work.
- Sir.

208
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,067
We almost didn't make it.

209
00:10:45,067 --> 00:10:47,633
Armed men ambushed us.

210
00:10:47,633 --> 00:10:48,867
There was an encounter, sir.

211
00:10:48,867 --> 00:10:50,667
They even held
Lieutenant Jacinto hostage.

212
00:10:51,267 --> 00:10:52,233
Hostage?

213
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,100
Are you alright, Lieutenant?

214
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:55,867
I'm okay. I'm okay, sir.

215
00:10:55,867 --> 00:10:57,200
But they managed to escape.

216
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,733
For sure, the Zafras did this

217
00:10:58,733 --> 00:11:00,567
because it's their gold!

218
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:03,700
Well, what's important
is that you're safe.

219
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:06,767
And you've secured the gold.

220
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:07,933
Well, sir,

221
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:09,200
based on the inventory,

222
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
a bag of jewelry is missing.

223
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,300
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- What? Missing?!

224
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:19,000
Umali, I want a full
investigation from the moment

225
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,167
it left the station
until after the ambush.

226
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:24,333
And until we establish that,

227
00:11:24,333 --> 00:11:27,967
everyone in the convoy
are persons of interest.

228
00:11:27,967 --> 00:11:30,000
- [UMALI SCOFFS]
- Is that clear?

229
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:30,967
Yes, sir.

230
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,700
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

231
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:36,233
[DOMINGO HUFFS]

232
00:11:36,233 --> 00:11:40,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

233
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,733
Sir.

234
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:44,733
The people you hired
were incompetent.

235
00:11:45,267 --> 00:11:46,267
Shut up!

236
00:11:46,267 --> 00:11:53,167
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:11:53,167 --> 00:11:54,167
[GLASS THUDS]

238
00:11:54,167 --> 00:11:55,100
Let's go.

239
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:57,300
Boss Mariano.

240
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,167
- Sir.
- He insisted on seeing you.

241
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,333
Let him in.

242
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:15,833
You have the guts to
show up here after failing, huh?

243
00:12:17,133 --> 00:12:20,833
In our world,
when you fail, you'll die.

244
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:23,967
No second chances.

245
00:12:23,967 --> 00:12:24,933
Hear me out.

246
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:28,033
I risked my life
just to get this.

247
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,167
[BAG THUDS]

248
00:12:36,133 --> 00:12:38,200
[ZIPPERS HISSING]

249
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,067
Boss.

250
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,233
Uh, our men called.

251
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:57,000
Those who were looking
for Sam Jacinto's body.

252
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,133
Did they find it?

253
00:12:58,733 --> 00:12:59,800
They got in trouble.

254
00:13:01,033 --> 00:13:02,067
Trouble?!

255
00:13:02,067 --> 00:13:03,400
Things got heated.

256
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,333
They fought with the locals.
There was a shootout.

257
00:13:06,333 --> 00:13:07,800
I specifically told them

258
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:11,233
to be discreet while searching.

259
00:13:11,233 --> 00:13:12,700
And now what?

260
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,433
They drew attention.

261
00:13:14,433 --> 00:13:17,000
Fine then. Tell them to move.

262
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,133
On it, boss.

263
00:13:23,400 --> 00:13:24,800
[LUCAS GRUNTS]

264
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,367
Why don't you just ask them
to come back here?

265
00:13:27,367 --> 00:13:29,367
We already lost
a lot of our men.

266
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:32,267
We cannot afford
to lose any more.

267
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:36,933
We're just wasting resources
looking for Samantha Jacinto!

268
00:13:36,933 --> 00:13:39,433
Ma, it's Papa
who's got problems!

269
00:13:40,367 --> 00:13:42,267
He doesn't trust me!

270
00:13:43,367 --> 00:13:46,233
He wanted proof
that I actually killed her!

271
00:13:46,233 --> 00:13:47,933
He used to be a cop.

272
00:13:48,433 --> 00:13:50,900
Of course, he'd want proof.

273
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,100
[LUCAS SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

274
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:54,900
But once he realizes
that he's wrong,

275
00:13:54,933 --> 00:13:56,267
he'll come around.

276
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:01,167
Don't worry too much about him.

277
00:14:01,167 --> 00:14:07,267
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:14:07,267 --> 00:14:09,000
[MUSIC FADES]

279
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,400
Here.

280
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:14,300
Gabo always gets himself
in trouble.

281
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:15,967
Dante, don't blame my son.

282
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:18,233
He gets into a fight

283
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:20,233
because he's probably
defending someone!

284
00:14:20,233 --> 00:14:21,333
I know my son!

285
00:14:21,333 --> 00:14:24,267
He doesn't get into a fight
just because!

286
00:14:24,267 --> 00:14:26,967
Can you take that outside?

287
00:14:26,967 --> 00:14:29,733
- I need to clean his wounds!
- Let's go.

288
00:14:35,267 --> 00:14:37,067
- Auntie, I'll do it.
- Alright.

289
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:49,233
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:56,267
What happened?
Who did you fight?

291
00:14:56,267 --> 00:14:57,800
We also don't know, Mister Rudy.

292
00:14:58,433 --> 00:15:00,800
[BONG] But, Mister Babot said...

293
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,500
They're looking for someone.

294
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,267
I think they're the ones looking
for Gloria!

295
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:08,200
[TEKLA]
I already told you, Mister Rudy.

296
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:11,200
That girl's full of bad luck!
Just look!

297
00:15:12,533 --> 00:15:15,133
This happened to Gabo
because of her!

298
00:15:15,133 --> 00:15:17,100
Tekla, let's stop
pointing fingers.

299
00:15:18,067 --> 00:15:20,033
Let's just wait
for my son to wake up!

300
00:15:21,367 --> 00:15:28,267
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

301
00:15:43,367 --> 00:15:50,233
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

302
00:16:05,333 --> 00:16:12,233
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

303
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:34,333
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

304
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,600
[MAMENG] Gloria, thank you.

305
00:16:58,233 --> 00:16:59,733
[GLORIA BREATHES DEEPLY]

306
00:16:59,733 --> 00:17:01,733
Auntie, you don't have
to thank me.

307
00:17:03,067 --> 00:17:06,133
Gabo is my husband.
I should take care of him.

308
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:10,200
Alright.

309
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:14,600
I'll bring out these clothes.

310
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:16,033
You just take care of him, okay?

311
00:17:17,767 --> 00:17:24,733
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,967
- [RUDY] How is it?
- Mameng.

313
00:17:32,967 --> 00:17:34,633
- [MAMENG] Uhh...
- How's my son?

314
00:17:34,633 --> 00:17:37,500
[MAMENG]
Gloria already cleaned up Gabo.

315
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,967
You don't have to worry.

316
00:17:39,967 --> 00:17:44,600
He doesn't have
serious injuries, just wounds.

317
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,200
His body's really just beat up.

318
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,767
That's good to hear.

319
00:17:48,667 --> 00:17:51,200
It'd be better for you
to get going.

320
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,300
[TOLITS] Come on, let's go home.

321
00:17:53,167 --> 00:17:55,000
- Thank you.
- Mister Rudy...

322
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,533
I'll be back tomorrow, okay?
I'll check on Gabo.

323
00:17:58,533 --> 00:18:00,133
- Okay.
- Alright, dear.

324
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:02,300
- Go on, it's getting late.
- [BINOY] Let's go, Tekla.

325
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:04,267
- [DANTE] Take care.
- [BINOY] Thank you.

326
00:18:05,667 --> 00:18:07,000
My gosh, Rudy.

327
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,667
I don't understand
what's happening to our family.

328
00:18:13,733 --> 00:18:17,200
Rudy keeps speaking nonsense.

329
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,233
He thinks he's always right!

330
00:18:19,233 --> 00:18:22,333
But if we followed
all his decisions,

331
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:26,033
then we'd be living
in a dumpster by now!

332
00:18:26,033 --> 00:18:32,033
Betchay, why are you
putting up with someone...

333
00:18:32,733 --> 00:18:36,033
...who does not care
about you?

334
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:40,200
- I know, I know!
- Why don't you look around?

335
00:18:41,667 --> 00:18:42,567
[BOTTLE CLINKS]

336
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,867
[PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

337
00:18:44,867 --> 00:18:47,600
Betchay, you're pathetic.

338
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,167
- You are with the wrong person.
- [BETCHAY CHUCKLES]

339
00:18:50,167 --> 00:18:51,600
'Cause you're the right person?

340
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,233
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

341
00:18:53,233 --> 00:18:55,067
Of course.

342
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:59,233
After all, why endure
on a hard floor

343
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:02,600
when you can lie on a soft bed?

344
00:19:04,733 --> 00:19:06,267
If you become mine...

345
00:19:06,267 --> 00:19:08,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

346
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:11,333
...I'll make you a queen.

347
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:20,100
I don't want to be a queen.
I want to be a princess.

348
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:23,233
Well, if that's the case,
then I'm the prince.

349
00:19:24,067 --> 00:19:25,067
Right?

350
00:19:25,067 --> 00:19:28,900
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

351
00:19:28,933 --> 00:19:29,933
Let's drink.

352
00:19:31,767 --> 00:19:33,600
Sir.

353
00:19:33,667 --> 00:19:36,767
I noticed something
during our encounter earlier.

354
00:19:36,767 --> 00:19:37,800
What is it?

355
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:38,900
[OBJECTS THUD]

356
00:19:39,667 --> 00:19:41,200
Sir.

357
00:19:41,267 --> 00:19:46,900
Organized groups, syndicates,
they don't work like that.

358
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:49,933
[SANTOS] I've noticed that too.

359
00:19:50,433 --> 00:19:52,433
They pretended
to crash into us

360
00:19:52,433 --> 00:19:54,300
- so they could steal the gold.
- Right?

361
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:57,367
Sir, it feels like...

362
00:19:59,167 --> 00:20:01,633
...the work of the thugs
of Ginintuang Lupa!

363
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:06,667
Could it be that the thieves
are from Ginintuang Lupa?

364
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:13,933
Paquito and his group of thugs
might be going against us.

365
00:20:13,933 --> 00:20:20,867
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

366
00:20:20,867 --> 00:20:23,667
- Someone should go with you.
- Ibyang!

367
00:20:23,667 --> 00:20:26,000
- Yeah? Go on, hurry.
- [PAQUITO] Ibyang!

368
00:20:26,967 --> 00:20:30,833
- What is it?
- Here. For you!

369
00:20:32,467 --> 00:20:34,433
- What's this?
<i> - Tapsilog!</i>

370
00:20:34,433 --> 00:20:36,667
- I bought it for you.
- What about mine?

371
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:38,100
Here's one for you, Matet.

372
00:20:38,833 --> 00:20:40,700
What did you do again?

373
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,200
- Come on, Ibyang.
- Come on!

374
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:48,000
He's trying to win your heart,
and here you are being rude.

375
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:51,033
- Is he your lawyer?
- [PAQUITO CHUCKLES]

376
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:53,400
But thank you!
You even got two.

377
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,467
- For "I love."
- Boss! Boss!

378
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,433
- So what happened?
- It failed, boss.

379
00:21:01,333 --> 00:21:04,167
- NLEA was prepared.
- Where's Django?

380
00:21:04,167 --> 00:21:05,400
He went to the Zafras.

381
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:07,767
Why'd he go there
when you failed?

382
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:12,100
Romy, you know Django.

383
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:16,133
He'll find a way
to fix the problem.

384
00:21:18,367 --> 00:21:20,033
I didn't see his face.

385
00:21:20,733 --> 00:21:23,100
Max. Want me to take you
to the hospital?

386
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:25,533
Just to check
if you have injuries.

387
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:26,733
I'm fine, sir.

388
00:21:27,333 --> 00:21:28,767
Lieutenant.

389
00:21:28,767 --> 00:21:32,300
Did you see the man's face?
Or any marks, at least?

390
00:21:34,267 --> 00:21:37,200
Didn't you see your hostage
taker carrying a bag?

391
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,200
I didn't!

392
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,367
It all happened so fast!
I--

393
00:21:39,367 --> 00:21:41,167
Lt. Jacinto.

394
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:43,333
We will escort you home.

395
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:45,033
I need to explain to your father

396
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:46,933
what happened
during the transfer.

397
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,000
Yes, sir.

398
00:21:58,067 --> 00:22:01,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

399
00:22:01,933 --> 00:22:03,267
[WHISPERS] Sir.

400
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:05,367
Do you have the bag?

401
00:22:06,233 --> 00:22:07,433
No!

402
00:22:07,433 --> 00:22:11,867
Once I find out who took it,

403
00:22:11,867 --> 00:22:14,233
that person is going to pay.

404
00:22:25,267 --> 00:22:26,200
Pa.

405
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,467
Good thing...

406
00:22:31,567 --> 00:22:34,100
my son is safe.

407
00:22:36,433 --> 00:22:38,033
If something bad
happened to him,

408
00:22:39,233 --> 00:22:41,933
I have no one to blame
but myself.

409
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:44,833
[RUDY SIGHS]

410
00:22:44,833 --> 00:22:47,400
Gloria, my son is a good man.

411
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:52,067
He just gets himself
in trouble all the time.

412
00:22:52,633 --> 00:22:54,367
He insists on...

413
00:22:54,367 --> 00:22:56,933
protecting other people.

414
00:22:56,933 --> 00:22:59,133
Especially those
who are defenseless.

415
00:23:00,933 --> 00:23:05,967
But this is what he gets.

416
00:23:07,467 --> 00:23:09,267
He always gets hurt.

417
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,333
I know, Pa.

418
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:16,267
Your son is a good man.

419
00:23:16,267 --> 00:23:18,233
My husband is a good man.

420
00:23:19,333 --> 00:23:24,133
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

421
00:23:24,167 --> 00:23:26,467
You should get some rest,
Gloria.

422
00:23:29,333 --> 00:23:30,967
Thank you, dear.

423
00:23:30,967 --> 00:23:37,867
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

424
00:23:53,400 --> 00:24:00,433
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

425
00:24:15,233 --> 00:24:22,233
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

426
00:24:37,233 --> 00:24:40,933
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

427
00:24:43,567 --> 00:24:44,433
- Boss Django.
- Boss Django.

428
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:49,033
Hey, Django.
What happened?

429
00:24:50,367 --> 00:24:55,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:24:55,533 --> 00:24:58,567
[PAQUITO] You messed up, Django!

431
00:25:00,367 --> 00:25:02,067
Sorry, Pa.

432
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:04,333
Umali's personnel
outnumbered us.

433
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:07,067
You faced Umali?

434
00:25:07,067 --> 00:25:09,067
Did they recognize you?

435
00:25:09,067 --> 00:25:10,100
Nope.

436
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:13,267
Well, good.

437
00:25:13,267 --> 00:25:15,667
We can't be complacent.

438
00:25:15,667 --> 00:25:17,433
I know Umali.

439
00:25:17,433 --> 00:25:20,500
He can trace this back to us.

440
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:22,167
But Boss Paquito,

441
00:25:22,167 --> 00:25:24,567
Boss Django held a
female NLEA agent hostage.

442
00:25:24,567 --> 00:25:28,133
Well, that doesn't matter.

443
00:25:28,133 --> 00:25:32,733
You failed to carry out
Boss Mariano's order.

444
00:25:32,733 --> 00:25:34,667
Don't worry.

445
00:25:34,667 --> 00:25:37,233
I'll make things right
with the Zafras.

446
00:25:37,267 --> 00:25:41,600
You've broken their trust, son.

447
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:43,700
You messed up big time!

448
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:45,667
[LAUGHS]

449
00:25:45,667 --> 00:25:48,433
I gave Mariano something.

450
00:25:48,433 --> 00:25:50,133
A bag of gold.

451
00:25:50,133 --> 00:25:52,500
That's what I'm talking about!

452
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:54,200
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

453
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:56,433
I think I've convinced him.

454
00:25:56,433 --> 00:25:59,700
If things work out,
we can walk away from Umali.

455
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:01,600
We'll be free.

456
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:05,233
We won't work for
the NLEA anymore.

457
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,600
I'll make Gabo eat dust.

458
00:26:09,633 --> 00:26:11,633
[LAUGHS]

459
00:26:11,633 --> 00:26:17,467
Then I'll win his wife, Gloria,
over with my money and wealth.

460
00:26:17,467 --> 00:26:19,400
[LAUGHS]

461
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:24,700
Don't count your blessings
before you receive them.

462
00:26:24,700 --> 00:26:26,100
You'll see, Pa.

463
00:26:27,133 --> 00:26:30,733
You'll see I'm right.

464
00:26:30,733 --> 00:26:32,567
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

465
00:26:32,567 --> 00:26:33,500
All right.

466
00:26:34,733 --> 00:26:36,200
- Oh.
- Cheers.

467
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:40,133
[INDISTINCT CHATTER, CHUCKLES]

468
00:26:42,567 --> 00:26:49,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

469
00:26:58,667 --> 00:27:00,300
[SAM]  I'm torn.

470
00:27:01,167 --> 00:27:03,600
<i> I can't think straight.</i>

471
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:07,767
<i>I'm investigating while
I'm hiding here in your home</i>

472
00:27:07,767 --> 00:27:12,500
<i>because I know you're the key
to clearing my name</i>

473
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:14,767
<i>and finally implicating
Victor Zafra</i>

474
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:18,233
<i> in all the cases against him.</i>

475
00:27:19,533 --> 00:27:25,067
<i>But as I slowly get to know
your family,</i>

476
00:27:25,067 --> 00:27:28,133
<i>I am also getting to know
who you are as well.</i>

477
00:27:28,133 --> 00:27:29,767
<i> The real you.</i>

478
00:27:30,533 --> 00:27:32,367
<i> I hope I was wrong.</i>

479
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:36,300
<i> I hope I was wrong about you.</i>

480
00:27:36,300 --> 00:27:39,200
<i>Because the person
in front of me...</i>

481
00:27:40,533 --> 00:27:42,700
<i> is a good man</i>

482
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:46,767
<i>with a pure heart
that wants to protect me.</i>

483
00:27:46,767 --> 00:27:53,733
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

484
00:28:09,167 --> 00:28:11,133
<i> My plan is underway.</i>

485
00:28:11,133 --> 00:28:16,167
<i>Team Alpha will slowly
turn against each other.</i>

486
00:28:16,167 --> 00:28:17,433
<i> How did the negotiation go?</i>

487
00:28:17,433 --> 00:28:19,133
<i>I will make them
sign a statement</i>

488
00:28:19,133 --> 00:28:21,267
so they won't pursue it further
<i> and we'll get off the hook.</i>

489
00:28:21,267 --> 00:28:22,400
<i> I'm counting on you, Max.</i>

490
00:28:22,433 --> 00:28:24,033
<i> I summoned Django.</i>

491
00:28:24,033 --> 00:28:25,967
<i> I'll have him finish the job.</i>

492
00:28:25,967 --> 00:28:27,100
<i> What about Lucas?</i>

493
00:28:27,100 --> 00:28:29,533
<i>He will lead Django
and his group.</i>

494
00:28:29,533 --> 00:28:30,967
<i> What happened last night?</i>

495
00:28:30,967 --> 00:28:32,667
<i>Damn it!
He has amnesia!</i>

496
00:28:32,667 --> 00:28:34,667
<i>Gabo.
Gabo, it's me. I'm your wife.</i>

497
00:28:34,667 --> 00:28:36,633
<i>- Cut it out, Tekla.
- Don't you remember?</i>

498
00:28:36,633 --> 00:28:39,100
<i>You don't remember?
You almost died last night.</i>

499
00:28:39,100 --> 00:28:40,367
<i> Gloria's in danger.</i>

500
00:28:40,367 --> 00:28:43,500
<i>The people after her
won't stop until she's dead.</i>

501
00:28:43,500 --> 00:28:46,667
<i>So we need to do everything
we can to help her.</i>

502
00:28:46,667 --> 00:28:48,700
<i>We're the only ones
who can protect her.</i>

503
00:28:48,700 --> 00:28:50,100
<i> We need to protect her.</i>

504
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:52,500
<i> We can't abandon her.</i>

505
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:57,933
<i>I think I'm getting too good
at pretending to be Gabo's wife.</i>

506
00:28:57,967 --> 00:28:59,233
<i> No.</i>

507
00:28:59,233 --> 00:29:00,400
<i> I'm doing fine.</i>

508
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:03,633
<i>This is the only way
I can keep my cover.</i>
